    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>And gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.6"/> elles be<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.7"/> cwicum mannum ciricgrið<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.8"/> abrocen sy, bete man georne be<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.9"/> þam þe seo dæd<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.10"/> sy, sy hit þurh feohtlac, si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.11"/> hit þurh reaflac, sig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.11"/> þurh þæt þe hi[t]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.12"/> sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif elles be cwycu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mannu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> cyricgryð abrocen sy, bete man georne beo þam þe seo dæde sie, sy hyt þurh feohtlac, sy hit þurh reaflac, sy þurh þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þe hit sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>Si uero aliter sine interfectione pax ęcclesię fracta sit, emendetur secundum quod acciderit, sit per pugnam sit per robariam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.6-2"/>, sit per id quod sit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Sin autem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.17"/> aliter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.18"/> de uiuis pax<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.19"/> ęcclesię uiolata fuerit uel pugnando<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.20"/> uel rapiendo uel per<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.21"/> quicquid sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#ICn_3.lnote.oe.22"/>,</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Si autem sine occisione pax ecclesie infracta fuerit, siue per pugnam siue per rapinam siue per malefactum, diligenter emendet iuxta modum ipsius malefacti:</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="156" ed="#robertson"/>And gyf elles be cwicum mannum<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#ICn_3.robnote.fn.4"/> ciricgrið abrocen sy, bete man georne be þam þe seo dæd sy, sy hit þurh feohtlac, si hit þurh reaflac, sig þurh þæt he hi[t]<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#ICn_3.robnote.fn.5"/> sy.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="234" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf elles be cwicum mannum ciricgrið abrocen sy, bete man georne be þam þe seo dæd sy, sy hit þurh feohtlac, si hit þurh reaflac, sig þurh þæt þe hit sy.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn sonst, [nämlich] im Falle der [angegriffene] Mensch leben bleibt, der Kirche Sonderfrieden gebrochen wird, büsse jener willig, je nachdem die Missethat ist, sei es durch Fechten, sei es durch Raub, sei es durch was es auch sei;</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if otherwise, [namely] where the [attacked] people stay alive, a church's protection is broken, let it be eagerly compensated according to what the deed is, whether by fighting or by robbery or by whatever it may be:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_3.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="157" ed="#robertson"/>And if the protection of the church is broken in some other respect, without the taking of life, amends shall diligently be made in accordance with the nature of the offence, whether it be fighting or robbery or whatever it may be.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="235" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if the sanctuary of the church is violated in some other way without the loss of life, penance shall be readily carried out according to the nature of the deed, whether it is violence or robbery or whatever it may be.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="283"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_4">VIII Atr 4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 4</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Northu_19">Northu 19</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="336"><label>corresponds to (reading)</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_4">VIII Atr 4</ref> <quote>When they differed, G's corresponded to the reading in Cnut's code (n. 339: VIII Atr 3, 4, 5:1, I Cn 2:5, 3, 3:2)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">G reads ‘hi’ for ‘hit’. Liebermann compares VIII Atr 4.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 283, October 2026 (MS Cons); AX: pages in Rabin (text / translation), checked against Rabin (page checked in his book), October 2026 (e.g. was “192”, now “234 / 235”; 6 rows of I Cn)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">be c. m. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">be c. m. lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyr. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyr. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">beo <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">beo Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dæde sie <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dæde sie Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hi <hi rend="italic">G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hi G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">282</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">robor. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">robor. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quodcumque <hi rend="italic">zu ergänzen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quodcumque to be supplied</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">de u. a. <hi rend="italic">Jo</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">de u. a. Jo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. f. p. e. <hi rend="italic">Lb Ct Jo</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. f. p. e. Lb Ct Jo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">purgando <hi rend="italic">Lb Ct Jo</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">purgando Lb Ct Jo</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quomodocunque <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> p. q. <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quomodocunque instead of p. q. Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_3.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">283</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fit <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fit Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_3.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VIII Atr. 4.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_3.robnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><label>mannum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">b. c. m.</hi> om. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_3.robnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><label>hi[t</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hi</hi> G.</seg></note>
